1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,772
Day 50: Jarvis, a voice assistant that needs no cloud AI.

2
00:00:05,222 --> 00:00:07,254
Jarvis runs only on local models.

3
00:00:07,254 --> 00:00:10,209
It keeps two memories: a diary of what happened,

4
00:00:10,209 --> 00:00:12,733
and a knowledge graph of what it learned.

5
00:00:13,183 --> 00:00:15,254
A cheap local check first asks:

6
00:00:15,254 --> 00:00:18,526
does the current conversation already cover this?

7
00:00:18,526 --> 00:00:19,929
No model call needed.

8
00:00:20,379 --> 00:00:23,453
If not, the diary searches past conversations,

9
00:00:23,453 --> 00:00:27,262
while the graph holds durable facts under three branches:

10
00:00:27,262 --> 00:00:28,866
user, directives, world.

11
00:00:29,316 --> 00:00:31,180
Each branch grows as a tree.

12
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:34,774
Past fifteen hundred tokens, a model splits a node and

13
00:00:34,774 --> 00:00:36,572
merges contradicting facts.

14
00:00:37,022 --> 00:00:40,965
Results land straight in the system prompt for the next reply,

15
00:00:40,965 --> 00:00:42,618
no extra tool call needed.

16
00:00:43,068 --> 00:00:46,589
The test run threw 135 failures and 367 errors.

17
00:00:46,589 --> 00:00:49,212
Every one traced back to speech and

18
00:00:49,212 --> 00:00:52,583
vector-search packages we skipped on purpose,

19
00:00:52,583 --> 00:00:54,306
not to the memory code.

20
00:00:54,756 --> 00:00:58,267
Full breakdown and three no-mock demo scripts are in the Zenn

21
00:00:58,267 --> 00:00:58,727
article.

22
00:00:58,727 --> 00:01:01,374
Free for non-commercial use; source on GitHub.
